# Security Policy - STFTP Industrial

## Verified Implementation
- Commit: 99c126e
- Test Vector: 11 blocks / 5500 bytes / SHA256 VERIFIED
- Overhead: +60 bytes per packet
- Encryption: AES-256-GCM (authenticated encryption)
- Integrity: SHA256 HMAC

## Security Assumptions

### 1. PSK Provisioning
- PSK MUST be 32 bytes (256-bit) random: `openssl rand -hex 32`
- PSK MUST be provisioned out-of-band (secure console, HSM, USB)
- NEVER hardcode PSK in public repository or firmware
- Each deployment MUST use unique PSK

### 2. Nonce Management
- Nonce MUST be 12 bytes: 4 random + 8 monotonic counter
- Nonce MUST NEVER repeat for same PSK
- Counter MUST persist in NVS/Flash across reboots
- Abort on counter overflow

### 3. Threat Model
Protects against: eavesdropping, tampering, replay, packet injection
Does NOT protect against: compromised PSK, physical access, weak RNG, DoS

### 4. Secure Deployment Checklist
- [ ] PSK generated with CSPRNG
- [ ] PSK stored in encrypted NVS
- [ ] Nonce persistence tested (10x power cycle)
- [ ] Wireshark confirms no cleartext
- [ ] Firewall restricts UDP port

